# The M5 PR 12 die blank: a unit cube with every edge blended at
# r = 0.12. Six shrunk planar faces, twelve quarter-cylinder blends,
# eight sphere-octant corner patches — the writer's hardest mixed
# case, since plane/cylinder/sphere faces here meet along TANGENT
# trimlines (straight ones and circular ones), not transverse ones.
#
# OCC splits the periodic corner-arc carriers at their seams, so its
# edge count exceeds the kernel's 48 (56 after the seam splits) while
# the vertex count stays at the kernel's 24 — the same accounting the
# ball and donut fixtures already record. (Wording fixed per the M7-1
# import review NOTE-7, issue #184: the old comment overclaimed on
# vertices.)
EXPECT_SOLIDS=1
EXPECT_SHELLS=1
EXPECT_FACES=26
EXPECT_EDGES=56
EXPECT_VERTICES=24
EXPECT_VOLUME_MM3=965231000
